[DONE] The Last Rite ends very quickly. Like, the enemies barely have time to spawn and move toward the caster before it’s over. It should be a bit more dramatic and lengthened.
    AN ARITHMETIC BUG WEARING A PACING COMPLAINT. `work` accrued at
    `1 + magic * 0.035` against a fixed 42, so the rite was 22s at magic 25 and
    SEVEN SECONDS at magic 150 — and the comment beside the constant claimed "42
    seconds at magic 25", which it had never been.
    The waves spawn 16-24 tiles out and have to WALK in. Measured on the old build:
    closest approach 4.3 tiles, peak inside the ring ZERO. Every gaunt the rite
    called was still crossing open ground when it finished. The scene could not
    happen at any skill level worth performing it at.
    Three changes. The base is 120 so there is a scene to have. The magic term is
    CAPPED at 2.0, because an unbounded multiplier against a fixed-length approach
    march can only end one way — skill now shortens the vigil rather than skipping
    it (99s at magic 6, 60s at magic 150). And the waves moved from thirds to
    fifths, four of them, so the last lands at 80% rather than on the closing tick.
    Measured after: 60s rite, first arrival at 17s, 43s of contested ring, four
    waves, 18 summoned, peaking at 6 inside the ring.
    THE ASSERTION THAT MATTERS is not "the rite is longer" — it is whether anything
    it summoned ARRIVES, which is what the report was actually about. tools/rites.js
    runs the real sim and watches the distances.

